"12.1 - Pointer Arithmetic"
---------------------------

"Pointer Arithmetic (Address Arithmetic)"
  - C supports three ways to access other elements:
    > Adding an integer to a pointer
    > Subtracting an integer from a pointer
    > Subtracting one pointer from another

  - Performing arithmetic on a pointer that doesn't point to an array element causes undefined behavior
